IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc11-investigation`

-- investigation: tests of ccc11-investigation.l4 (Part VIII.1, sections 320.27 to 320.3: demands, samples, warrants, testing blood)
-- Expected values are written by hand from the text of the provision, beside each assertion, before the run; none is copied from the code's output.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING: the text says yes / the text says no in its own words / not covered.


§ `s 320.27(1): demands on reasonable suspicion (a power: every gate unmet is NOT COVERED, never "the officer may not")`
-- arguments for (a): peace officer (by s 2) ; reasonable grounds to suspect alcohol or a drug ; reasonable grounds to suspect operation within three hours
#ASSERT `s 320.27(1)(a) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately perform the physical coordination tests prescribed by regulation and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- peace officer, both suspicions
#ASSERT `s 320.27(1)(a) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately perform the physical coordination tests prescribed by regulation and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a peace officer: the grant is the peace officer's
#ASSERT `s 320.27(1)(a) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately perform the physical coordination tests prescribed by regulation and to accompany the peace officer` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- peace officer status not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.27(1)(a) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately perform the physical coordination tests prescribed by regulation and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no reasonable grounds to suspect alcohol or a drug
#ASSERT `s 320.27(1)(a) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately perform the physical coordination tests prescribed by regulation and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no reasonable grounds to suspect operation within the preceding three hours
-- arguments for (b): peace officer ; suspect alcohol ; suspect operation within three hours ; the device is an approved screening device (by s 320.11)
#ASSERT `s 320.27(1)(b) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately provide samples of breath for an approved screening device and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- alcohol suspected, approved screening device
#ASSERT `s 320.27(1)(b) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately provide samples of breath for an approved screening device and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a suspicion of alcohol ("in the case of alcohol")
#ASSERT `s 320.27(1)(b) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately provide samples of breath for an approved screening device and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the device is not an approved screening device
#ASSERT `s 320.27(1)(b) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately provide samples of breath for an approved screening device and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the device is approved is not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.27(1)(b) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately provide samples of breath for an approved screening device and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a peace officer
#ASSERT `s 320.27(1)(b) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately provide samples of breath for an approved screening device and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no suspicion of operation within three hours
-- arguments for (c): peace officer ; suspect a drug ; suspect operation within three hours ; the equipment is approved drug screening equipment (by s 320.11)
#ASSERT `s 320.27(1)(c) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately provide samples of a bodily substance for approved drug screening equipment and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a drug suspected, approved drug screening equipment
#ASSERT `s 320.27(1)(c) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately provide samples of a bodily substance for approved drug screening equipment and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a suspicion of a drug ("in the case of a drug")
#ASSERT `s 320.27(1)(c) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately provide samples of a bodily substance for approved drug screening equipment and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the equipment is not approved
#ASSERT `s 320.27(1)(c) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person to immediately provide samples of a bodily substance for approved drug screening equipment and to accompany the peace officer` NOTHING TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- peace officer status not covered

§ `s 320.27(2): mandatory alcohol screening: no suspicion needed, but an approved screening device in hand, a lawful exercise of powers, and a person operating a motor vehicle`
-- arguments: peace officer ; has an approved screening device in possession (by s 320.11) ; in the course of the lawful exercise of powers ; the person is operating a motor vehicle (by s 2)
#ASSERT `s 320.27(2) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person who is operating a motor vehicle to immediately provide samples of breath for an approved screening device` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- all gates
#ASSERT `s 320.27(2) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person who is operating a motor vehicle to immediately provide samples of breath for an approved screening device` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in the course of the lawful exercise of powers
#ASSERT `s 320.27(2) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person who is operating a motor vehicle to immediately provide samples of breath for an approved screening device` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no approved screening device in possession
#ASSERT `s 320.27(2) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person who is operating a motor vehicle to immediately provide samples of breath for an approved screening device` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not operating a motor vehicle
#ASSERT `s 320.27(2) the peace officer may, by demand, require the person who is operating a motor vehicle to immediately provide samples of breath for an approved screening device` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- peace officer status not covered

§ `s 320.28(1): demands on reasonable grounds to believe, for breath or blood, by a peace officer`
-- arguments for (a)(i): peace officer ; believe impaired by alcohol ; believe committed 320.14(1)(b) ; as soon as practicable ; approved instrument ; qualified technician (breath)
#ASSERT `s 320.28(1)(a)(i) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- grounds to believe impaired, as soon as practicable, approved instrument, qualified technician
#ASSERT `s 320.28(1)(a)(i) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- grounds to believe the 320.14(1)(b) offence was committed
#ASSERT `s 320.28(1)(a)(i) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither ground
#ASSERT `s 320.28(1)(a)(i) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- demand not made as soon as practicable
#ASSERT `s 320.28(1)(a)(i) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an approved instrument
#ASSERT `s 320.28(1)(a)(i) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- qualified technician not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.28(1)(a)(i) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a peace officer
-- arguments for (a)(ii): peace officer ; believe impaired ; believe committed (1)(b) ; as soon as practicable ; grounds to believe incapable of providing breath or impracticable ; qualified medical practitioner ; qualified technician (blood)
#ASSERT `s 320.28(1)(a)(ii) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- blood, a qualified medical practitioner takes it
#ASSERT `s 320.28(1)(a)(ii) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- blood, a qualified technician takes it
#ASSERT `s 320.28(1)(a)(ii) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no grounds to believe the person cannot give breath: blood is not available
#ASSERT `s 320.28(1)(a)(ii) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither a practitioner nor a technician takes it
#ASSERT `s 320.28(1)(a)(ii) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither ground of belief
-- arguments for (b): peace officer ; believe impaired ; believe committed (1)(b) ; as soon as practicable
#ASSERT `s 320.28(1)(b) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to accompany the peace officer for the purpose of taking samples of breath or blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- to accompany for the taking of samples
#ASSERT `s 320.28(1)(b) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to accompany the peace officer for the purpose of taking samples of breath or blood` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no ground of belief
#ASSERT `s 320.28(1)(b) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to accompany the peace officer for the purpose of taking samples of breath or blood` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not as soon as practicable

§ `s 320.28(2) and (3): drug demands, and the evaluating officer's breath demand`
-- arguments for (2)(a): peace officer ; believe impaired by a drug or a combination ; believe committed 320.14(1)(c), (d) or (4) ; as soon as practicable ; evaluating officer (by s 320.11)
#ASSERT `s 320.28(2)(a) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to submit to an evaluation conducted by an evaluating officer and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- grounds to believe impaired by a drug, an evaluating officer
#ASSERT `s 320.28(2)(a) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to submit to an evaluation conducted by an evaluating officer and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- grounds to believe a drug offence was committed
#ASSERT `s 320.28(2)(a) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to submit to an evaluation conducted by an evaluating officer and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither ground
#ASSERT `s 320.28(2)(a) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to submit to an evaluation conducted by an evaluating officer and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the officer is not an evaluating officer
#ASSERT `s 320.28(2)(a) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to submit to an evaluation conducted by an evaluating officer and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not as soon as practicable
-- arguments for (2)(b): peace officer ; believe impaired ; believe committed ; as soon as practicable ; qualified medical practitioner ; qualified technician (blood)
#ASSERT `s 320.28(2)(b) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- blood taken by a practitioner
#ASSERT `s 320.28(2)(b) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- blood taken by a technician
#ASSERT `s 320.28(2)(b) the peace officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood and to accompany the peace officer` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither
-- arguments for (3): evaluating officer ; suspect alcohol ; a demand was not made under (1) ; as soon as practicable ; approved instrument ; qualified technician
#ASSERT `s 320.28(3) the evaluating officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- all gates
#ASSERT `s 320.28(3) the evaluating officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- a demand was made under subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 320.28(3) the evaluating officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no reasonable grounds to suspect alcohol
#ASSERT `s 320.28(3) the evaluating officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an evaluating officer
#ASSERT `s 320.28(3) the evaluating officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of breath for an approved instrument` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the instrument is approved is not covered

§ `s 320.28(4) and (5): after an evaluation, identifying the drug (a duty), the demands for oral fluid, urine or blood (powers), and the types of drugs`
#ASSERT `s 320.28(4) the evaluating officer shall identify the type or types of drugs in question` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- grounds to believe a listed drug is impairing: the officer shall identify it
#ASSERT `s 320.28(4) the evaluating officer shall identify the type or types of drugs in question` FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the "if" is unmet
-- arguments for (4)(a): evaluating officer ; grounds to believe a listed drug is impairing ; as soon as practicable
#ASSERT `s 320.28(4)(a) the evaluating officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide a sample of oral fluid or urine` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- oral fluid or urine
#ASSERT `s 320.28(4)(a) the evaluating officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide a sample of oral fluid or urine` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no grounds
#ASSERT `s 320.28(4)(a) the evaluating officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide a sample of oral fluid or urine` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an evaluating officer
-- arguments for (4)(b): evaluating officer ; grounds ; as soon as practicable ; practitioner ; technician
#ASSERT `s 320.28(4)(b) the evaluating officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- blood taken by a practitioner
#ASSERT `s 320.28(4)(b) the evaluating officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- blood taken by a technician
#ASSERT `s 320.28(4)(b) the evaluating officer may, by demand made as soon as practicable, require the person to provide samples of blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither
#ASSERT `s 320.28(5) the type of drug is one of the types of drugs for the purpose of subsection 320.28(4)` `s 320.28(5)(a) a depressant` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 320.28(5) the type of drug is one of the types of drugs for the purpose of subsection 320.28(4)` `s 320.28(5)(b) an inhalant` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 320.28(5) the type of drug is one of the types of drugs for the purpose of subsection 320.28(4)` `s 320.28(5)(c) a dissociative anaesthetic` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 320.28(5) the type of drug is one of the types of drugs for the purpose of subsection 320.28(4)` `s 320.28(5)(d) cannabis` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- (d)
#ASSERT `s 320.28(5) the type of drug is one of the types of drugs for the purpose of subsection 320.28(4)` `s 320.28(5)(e) a stimulant` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- (e)
#ASSERT `s 320.28(5) the type of drug is one of the types of drugs for the purpose of subsection 320.28(4)` `s 320.28(5)(f) a hallucinogen` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- (f)
#ASSERT `s 320.28(5) the type of drug is one of the types of drugs for the purpose of subsection 320.28(4)` `s 320.28(5)(g) a narcotic analgesic` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- (g)
#ASSERT `s 320.28(5) the type of drug is one of the types of drugs for the purpose of subsection 320.28(4)` `s 320.28(5) a type of drug that is none of those` EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- "the types of drugs are the following": any other type is not one

§ `s 320.28(6) to (10): who may take blood, the container, the retained sample, validity, release of the retained sample`
-- arguments for (6): taker is a qualified medical practitioner ; a qualified technician ; satisfied that taking the sample would not endanger the health
#ASSERT `s 320.28(6) a sample of blood may be taken from the person under section 320.28` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a practitioner, satisfied
#ASSERT `s 320.28(6) a sample of blood may be taken from the person under section 320.28` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a technician, satisfied
#ASSERT `s 320.28(6) a sample of blood may be taken from the person under section 320.28` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not satisfied: "only if they are satisfied"
#ASSERT `s 320.28(6) a sample of blood may be taken from the person under section 320.28` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- neither: "only by a qualified medical practitioner or a qualified technician"
#ASSERT `s 320.28(6) a sample of blood may be taken from the person under section 320.28` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- practitioner status not covered and not a technician
#ASSERT `s 320.28(6) a sample of blood may be taken from the person under section 320.28` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a technician, whatever the practitioner answer
-- arguments for (7): received into an approved container (by s 320.11) ; the container was subsequently sealed
#ASSERT `s 320.28(7) the duty to receive the sample of blood into an approved container and to seal it has been met` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- received into an approved container and sealed
#ASSERT `s 320.28(7) the duty to receive the sample of blood into an approved container and to seal it has been met` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not sealed
#ASSERT `s 320.28(7) the duty to receive the sample of blood into an approved container and to seal it has been met` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not an approved container
#ASSERT `s 320.28(7) the duty to receive the sample of blood into an approved container and to seal it has been met` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether it is an approved container is not covered
-- arguments for (8): samples of blood taken under this section ; one of the samples was retained
#ASSERT `s 320.28(8) the duty to cause one of the samples to be retained has been met` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- retained
#ASSERT `s 320.28(8) the duty to cause one of the samples to be retained has been met` TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not retained
#ASSERT `s 320.28(8) the duty to cause one of the samples to be retained has been met` FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no samples taken under this section: the duty does not arise
#ASSERT `s 320.28(8) the person who takes samples of blood shall cause one to be retained` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED   -- no samples taken under this section, no duty
#TRACE `s 320.28(8) the person who takes samples of blood shall cause one to be retained` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 320.28 a person who takes samples of blood under section 320.28` DOES `s 320.28(8) cause one of the samples of blood to be retained for the purpose of analysis by or on behalf of the person from whom they were taken` AT 1
#ASSERT `s 320.28(9) a failure to comply with subsection 320.28(7) or (8) by itself affects the validity of the taking of the sample or of an analysis made of it` TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- a failure does not by itself affect validity
#ASSERT `s 320.28(9) a failure to comply with subsection 320.28(7) or (8) by itself affects the validity of the taking of the sample or of an analysis made of it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no failure: the subsection is silent
-- arguments for (10): a summary application of the person from whom samples were taken ; a sample was retained ; the day the samples were taken ; the day the application is made
#ASSERT `s 320.28(10) the judge shall order the release of the retained sample to the person` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 9 2026) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- the last day of the six months
#ASSERT `s 320.28(10) the judge shall order the release of the retained sample to the person` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 8 2026) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- inside the six months
#ASSERT `s 320.28(10) the judge shall order the release of the retained sample to the person` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 9 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the day after the six months: outside the period the text fixes
#ASSERT `s 320.28(10) the judge shall order the release of the retained sample to the person` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not a summary application of that person
#ASSERT `s 320.28(10) the judge shall order the release of the retained sample to the person` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no sample was retained
#ASSERT `s 320.28(10) the judge shall order the release of the retained sample to the person` TRUE TRUE (Date 31 8 2026) (Date 3 3 2027) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- six months from 31 August is "31 February" 2027, rolled forward to 3 March (fork F11)
#ASSERT `s 320.28(10) the judge shall order the release of the retained sample to the person` TRUE TRUE (Date 31 8 2026) (Date 4 3 2027) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the day after
#ASSERT `s 320.28(10) the judge shall order the release of the retained sample` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED   -- no application, no duty
#TRACE `s 320.28(10) the judge shall order the release of the retained sample` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a judge` DOES `s 320.28(10) order the release of the retained sample to the person, subject to any terms that the judge considers appropriate` AT 1

§ `s 320.29: warrants to obtain blood samples`
-- arguments for (1): a justice (by s 2) ; satisfied on an information on oath in Form 1 ; grounds to believe operated within eight hours ; the accident resulted in bodily harm (by s 2) ; or in the death of another person ; grounds to suspect alcohol or a drug ; practitioner: unable to consent ; practitioner: will not endanger health
#ASSERT `s 320.29(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician to take the samples of the person’s blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- all gates, bodily harm
#ASSERT `s 320.29(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician to take the samples of the person’s blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- all gates, a death
#ASSERT `s 320.29(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician to take the samples of the person’s blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a death, whatever the bodily harm answer
#ASSERT `s 320.29(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician to take the samples of the person’s blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither bodily harm nor death
#ASSERT `s 320.29(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician to take the samples of the person’s blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE NOTHING FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- bodily harm not covered and no death
#ASSERT `s 320.29(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician to take the samples of the person’s blood` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the justice is not satisfied on an information on oath
#ASSERT `s 320.29(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician to take the samples of the person’s blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no reasonable grounds to believe operation within the preceding eight hours
#ASSERT `s 320.29(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician to take the samples of the person’s blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no reasonable grounds to suspect alcohol or a drug
#ASSERT `s 320.29(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician to take the samples of the person’s blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the practitioner is not of the opinion that the person is unable to consent
#ASSERT `s 320.29(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician to take the samples of the person’s blood` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the practitioner is not of the opinion that the sampling will not endanger health
#ASSERT `s 320.29(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician to take the samples of the person’s blood` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a justice
#ASSERT `s 320.29(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer to require a qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician to take the samples of the person’s blood` NOTHING TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- justice status not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.29(2) the warrant may be in Form 5, varied to suit the case` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a warrant issued under (1)
#ASSERT `s 320.29(2) the warrant may be in Form 5, varied to suit the case` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a warrant under (1): not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.29(3) as the text shows it`  EQUALS "(3) [Repealed, 2022, c. 17, s. 10]"   -- the text shows (3) repealed
#ASSERT `s 320.29(4) samples of blood may be taken from the person under the warrant at this time` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- while the practitioner is satisfied the conditions continue
#ASSERT `s 320.29(4) samples of blood may be taken from the person under the warrant at this time` FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- "only during the time that"
#ASSERT `s 320.29(5) the peace officer shall give a copy of the warrant and a notice in Form 5.1 to the person from whom the samples of blood are taken` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- the warrant is executed: the peace officer shall give a copy and a notice
#ASSERT `s 320.29(5) the peace officer shall give a copy of the warrant and a notice in Form 5.1 to the person from whom the samples of blood are taken` FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not executed: the duty does not arise
#ASSERT `s 320.29(5) the peace officer shall give the person a copy of the warrant and a notice` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED   -- not executed, no duty
#TRACE `s 320.29(5) the peace officer shall give the person a copy of the warrant and a notice` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `s 320.29(5) give a copy of the warrant and a notice in Form 5.1, varied to suit the case, to the person from whom the samples of blood are taken` AT 1
#ASSERT `s 320.29(6) subsections 320.28(7) to (10) apply to the taking of the samples of blood` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- samples taken under a warrant of this section
#ASSERT `s 320.29(6) subsections 320.28(7) to (10) apply to the taking of the samples of blood` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not under this section: not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.3 the samples may be analyzed to determine the person’s blood alcohol concentration or blood drug concentration, or both` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- blood taken for the purposes of this Part may be analysed
#ASSERT `s 320.3 the samples may be analyzed to determine the person’s blood alcohol concentration or blood drug concentration, or both` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- blood not taken for the purposes of this Part: not covered

